        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(line): cap user profile cache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where long-running LINE gateways could accumulate an unbounded in-process user profile cache, increasing memory use over time when many distinct users are resolved.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a 1024-entry cap to the LINE plugin's `userProfileCache` using `pruneMapToMaxSize`, with LRU refresh on cache hits. Matches the bounded-cache pattern used in other channel plugins.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators running LINE channels on long-lived gateways get bounded memory for profile lookups. Normal workloads are unchanged; only the oldest cached profiles are evicted under sustained high-cardinality traffic.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.extension-line.config.ts extensions/line/src/send.test.ts` — 16 tests passed\n- New eviction test verifies the oldest profile entry is re-fetched after the cap is exceeded\n\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
